Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='nopdf', at=datetime(2026, 10, 9, 0, 0, 0), actor='owner', title='There is no PDF document; typst only draws what the core priced', body='- A block\'s fulfillment is written in by the core and typst only DRAWS it (no `evalSpec`/`priorityFromTime` in typst since 2026-09-02). It is the entry\'s `value`, so the number on a page, in a block and in a briefing is one `prodrome_core::view::entries` call. `suzatary todos open` prices with the same function. There is no PDF document since 2026-10-09 (the owner: "We don\'t need the pdfs anymore").\n- *There is no document build* (2026-10-09): the PDF, `suzatary pdf`, its smoke and the typst templates are deleted; the repository releases the program. `.#triage` carries typst and the fonts for the pages, the site and the guide.\n- *A record is shown as a block* (`suzatary_core::decoration`): `raise_block` prints it as `#kind(fields)[body]`, and typst is READ with typst\'s own parser (`typst-syntax`; a hand parser is a second reading) only to check that a write renders as what was built. The document tree over the blocks went with the PDF (2026-10-09); nothing reads a block back into a record.', rationale='Typst stopped computing fulfillment on 2026-09-02. The owner, 2026-10-09: "We don\'t need the pdfs anymore".', supersedes=()))